  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1210 PM CDT Fri Jul 3 2026\n\nHighs in the mid 90s and dew points in the mid 70s combines for\nHI's to max out close to 110 degrees again today, with the \nprolonged duration of dangerously high heat and humidity keeping\nthe Excessive Heat Warning in effect one more day. We \ntransition to a Heat Advisory for Independence Day, as highs are\ngenerally expected in the lower half 90s so HI's top off closer\nto around 105 degrees. By the beginning of the new week, \nthey've backed off enough to return temps/humidity levels closer\nto our seasonal norms for mid summer.\n\nDaily pcpn chances increase with time and mostly maximize \nduring the peak heating hours of the afternoon and early \nevening. This helps with the ridge's breakdown, and with\nadditional cloud/debris from daily rising pops, the combo should\nassist temps to return to more common/seasonal averages for \nthis time of year. Of course still high PW's means locally heavy\nrains are possible, in addition to lightning and brief gusty \nwinds, with any stronger storms that arise.",
